# CVEs with no upstream fix in the Debian trixie base image, or in build-time
# Python tools removed from the runtime image.
#
# The intentional Flask==1.0.0 / Werkzeug==0.14.1 / Jinja2==2.10 CVEs are
# NOT listed here — they keep the CI gate permanently red by design.

# ── zlib1g / libsqlite3-0 (pre-existing, will_not_fix) ──────────────────────
CVE-2023-45853
CVE-2025-7458

# ── util-linux family: libblkid integer overflow (affected, no fix) ──────────
# Affects: bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
#          libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux
CVE-2026-53615

# ── gzip: LZH decompression buffer overflow (affected, no fix) ───────────────
CVE-2026-41992

# ── libacl1: symlink traversal in libacl functions (affected, no fix) ────────
CVE-2026-54369

# ── ncurses: buffer overflow (affected, no fix) ───────────────────────────────
# Affects: libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin
CVE-2025-69720

# ── jaraco.context: path traversal via tar archives ──────────────────────────
# Transitive dependency of pip/setuptools — not installed by requirements.txt
# and not present in the runtime image (wheel and jaraco.context are uninstalled
# in the Dockerfile after pip completes).
CVE-2026-23949

# ── wheel: code execution via malicious wheel file ───────────────────────────
# Build-time tool uninstalled from the runtime image in the Dockerfile.
CVE-2026-24049
